        "date": "2026-11-12T01:59:21Z"
      },
      "message": "test(app): the STEP bore's heavy test pins platform-robust facts\n\nThe bore's exact pins (one rings level at Z 20.000; 5530 / 5497 / 600)\nnever held on macOS: on the same commit ecb54b7f, macOS (Apple silicon)\nplans 5786 / 5753 / 651 against the Windows measure, deterministically -\nlast-place platform float (most likely libm) under knife-edge planner\ndecisions (#882, #982), filed as #1010. Bisect on macOS puts the second\nrings level (Z 10.000, crossing) at the #689 merge (STEP chord cap and\narc fit), which changed the bore's mesh and arcs and was not re-measured\nin the heavy lane.\n\nEvery safety assertion stays: no verifier warning, no budget refusal,\nevery rings level named. The exact pins become: Z 20.000 goes to the\nrings, a rings level only for a crossing, at most two of five levels on\nthe rings, arcs posted, 5000..=8000 moves with >= 98 % planar feeds.\nDecision in docs/decisions/984-bore-heavy-pins.md.\n\nFixes #984\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
      "tree": {
